    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Unstable Compounds",
      "category": "defensive",
      "text": "When an attacker scores a critical hit against the reckless scientist, one of the scientist's poorly stowed alchemical items bursts. The GM determines the item randomly. If it was a bomb, the scientist takes damage from the bomb, and any creature adjacent to the scientist takes the splash damage. Any other item is simply wasted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Quick Bomber",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "The reckless scientist Interacts to draw a bomb, then Strikes with it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Reckless Alchemy",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "Requirements The reckless scientist is holding a bomb or elixir\n\n---\n\nEffect The reckless scientist combines the bomb with another bomb or the elixir with another elixir. They can Interact to draw a second bomb or elixir if necessary as part of this action. They attempt a DC 28 Crafting check check, destroying both component items to create one new item. If a viable resulting item isn't used by the end of the scientist's next turn, it explodes as described under critical failure.\n\n---\n\nCritical Success The new item has the full effect of both component items when used.\n\nSuccess The new item combines both items, but halves the effect of each. (This halves damage for bombs, the amount of healing of elixirs of life, or the duration for effects that can't have their value halved. Details are determined by the GM.)\n\nFailure The new item is inert.\n\nCritical Failure The new item immediately explodes, dealing 3d6 piercing damage to the reckless scientist."
    }
